.env
output/
# data/state.db IS tracked — it's the GitHub Actions cloud-tick workflow's
# only persistence between ephemeral runs (see .github/workflows/pipeline.yml
# and cmd_cloud_tick in cli.py). Its `tokens` table is scrubbed (DELETE FROM
# tokens) before every commit — never let a real access/refresh token reach
# this file in a commit, this repo is public.
#
# One database per account profile (see src/config.py). Each is listed here
# explicitly rather than as !data/state*.db, so a scratch database such as
# state_test.db can never be swept into a commit. scripts/scrub_tokens.py
# scrubs every data/state*.db regardless.
data/*
!data/state.db
!data/state_terraria.db
assets/backgrounds/
assets/voices/
src/out/
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
